  "problem": "The solution of the system of linear equations\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}2x+y+1=0 \\\\ 4x+3y-3=0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\ngives the point where the highways meet. This solution can be written in matrix form as\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}]=\\frac{1}{2}[\\begin{aligned}a & b \\\\ -4 & 2\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ c\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nFind the values of $a,$ $b,$ and $c.$\n\n                            \n                                    \n                                        \n                                            \n\n                                                \n\n                                        \n                                        \n                                        \n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                        $a\\,=$\n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                            \n                                        {{field-1}}                \n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                        \n$\\,b\\,=$\n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                            \n                                        {{field-2}}                \n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                        \n$\\,c\\,=$\n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                            \n                                        {{field-3}}",
  "worked_solution": "This system can be written as\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}2 & 1 \\\\ 4 & 3\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nTo find the solution, we need to calculate the inverse of the coefficient matrix $A=[\\begin{aligned}2 & 1 \\\\ 4 & 3\\end{aligned}].$ This gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}^{-1} & =\\frac{1}{2\\cdot 3-4\\cdot 1}[\\begin{aligned}3 & -1 \\\\ -4 & 2\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}[\\begin{aligned}3 & -1 \\\\ -4 & 2\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we can write the solution to this system as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x & ={A}^{-1}b \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}[\\begin{aligned}3 & -1 \\\\ -4 & 2\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$",
